<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.74 million bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.74 million bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run Cotton Export Corporation of Pakistan (CEC) said on Monday 1996/97 (July-June) cotton output had reached a provisional 8.744 million 375-lb bales by Thursday, down from 9.947 million at the same time a year ago.</p>
<p>Delivery and ginning figures in million bales (year-ago):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.660 (8.175)  2.084 (1.771)  8.744 (9.947)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.655 (8.174)  2.084 (1.771)  8.739 (9.946)</p>
<p> Mill sales     5.950 (6.951)  1.944 (1.274)  7.895 (8.225)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.008 (1.023)  0.014 (0.471)  0.022 (1.494)</p>
<p> CEC		nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)</p>
<p> Unsold	   0.701 (0.200)  0.125 (0.026)  0.826 (0.226)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
